# Cache policy for Cloudflare Workers static assets.
#
# Rules here must not overlap: when several match a request, Cloudflare *joins* the
# duplicate headers with a comma instead of letting the more specific one win. The
# two prefixes below are disjoint, and both are content-addressed, so freezing them
# is safe:
#   _framework/  — every file carries a fingerprint (dotnet.native.<hash>.wasm, and
#                  one hashed .wasm per assembly); verified: no unhashed file exists.
#   package_*    — the Uno shell bundle, hashed as a whole. The bundled fonts live
#                  inside it (WasmCSS/Fonts.css loads them by relative path), so they
#                  are already covered and must not get a second `/*.ttf` rule.
#
# Everything at the root — index.html, service-worker.js, manifest.webmanifest — is
# deliberately left to the Workers default, `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`, so a
# new deploy is picked up on the next visit instead of being pinned by a stale shell.

/_framework/*
  Cache-Control: public, immutable, max-age=31536000

/package_*
  Cache-Control: public, immutable, max-age=31536000
